Test_suspend() and Test_suspend_autocmd() wait for shell prompts that match
[$#] $.  An exported PS1 from the test environment can make /bin/sh use a
longer prompt that does not match that pattern.  Then the prompt wait times
out silently before the test sends "fg".

Unset PS1 so the shell started by the test uses its default prompt.


--- vim-9.2.0670/src/testdir/test_suspend.vim
+++ vim-9.2.0670/src/testdir/test_suspend.vim
@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 " Test :suspend
 
+silent! unlet $PS1
+
 func CheckSuspended(buf, fileExists)
   call WaitForAssert({-> assert_match('[$#] $', term_getline(a:buf, '.'))})
 
